# The service-switch test (tests/service-switch/service_switch.py drives it):
# system generations switch running services through procmgr.
# - lexicon.svc: (replace transparent), a service with no hardware or
#   firmware state (its clients' channels end and they reconnect): switched,
#   rolled back after a failed health window, and back to the image.
# - clock.svc: (replace graceful), it must quiesce on Stop; it does not
#   handle Stop, so a switch is refused and it keeps running (never ended to
#   make way).
# - The ACPI pair is not here: its restart contract is reboot until its
#   stop, rebind and health handshake is validated (coordination with the
#   ACPI agent, 2026-11-07).
# Plus the LAN remote session with builds granted, its work root on the
# system volume, and a desktop, so the person's "Allow app replacement"
# switch can be turned on by a click (ccl-remote's display-capture grant
# shows that section).
(startup v1
  (start "logstore.svc" (priority 5))
  (start "clock.svc" (priority 5) (replace graceful))
  (start "display.svc" (priority 5))
  (start "desktop.svc" (priority 4))
  (start "lexicon.svc" (priority 4) (replace transparent))
  (start "ccl-remote.app" (priority 4) (network approve-declared) (display-capture approve-declared)
    (arguments (Remote_Parameters listen => Remote_Listen.LAN
      display => Pairing_Display.Kernel_Console work => "@system/work"
      files => true builds => true mail => true)))
)
